      "text": "Given the polynomial equation $x^3+3x^2+4x-11=0$ has roots $a$, $b$, and $c$, by Vieta's formulas:\n- $a+b+c = -3$\n- $ab+bc+ca = 4$\n- $abc = 11$\n\nSince the roots of the new polynomial equation are $a+b$, $b+c$, and $c+a$, we use Vieta's formulas again to find the sum and the products of these new roots.\n\nAdding the original roots: \n\\[\n(a+b) + (b+c) + (c+a) = a+b+c + 2(a+b+c) = -3\n\\]\n\\[\n-3 + 2(-3) = -3\n\\]\n\nNow, calculating the sum of the products:\n\\[\n(a+b)(b+c) + (b+c)(c+a) + (c+a)(a+b)\n\\]\nUsing the identity:\n\\[\nab + bc + ca + ab + bc + ac = 4 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad 2(ab + bc + ca) = 4 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad ab + bc + ca = 2\n\\]\n\nExpanding the product:\n\\[\n(a+b)(b+c) = ab + ac + b^2 + bc \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad (a+b)(b+c) = b(ab + bc + ca) + ac = 2b^2 + 4b\n\\]\n\\[\n(b+c)(c+a) = bc + ca + c^2 + ab \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad (b+c)(c+a) = c(bc + ca + ab) + b = c(a-b)^2 + b\n\\]\n\\[\n(c+a)(a+b) = cab + ab + a^2 + c^2 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad (c+a)(a+b) = c(ab + bc + ca) + a = c(2+ab) + a\n\\]\n\nAdding these up:\n\\[\na+b+b+c+c+a = 2a + 2b + 2c\n\\]\n\\[\na+b+c + 2(a+b+c) = -3\n\\]\n\\[\n5(a+b+c) = -3 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad 5(-3) = -3\n\\]\n\nThe sum of products of pairs:\n\\[\nab+bc+ac = ab + bc + ca = 2\n\\]\n\nNow, to determine the total product $t$:\n\\[\nt = (a+b)(b+c)(c+a)\n\\]\nUsing $(a+b)(b+c)(c+a)$ formula:\n\\[\n(a+b)(b+c)(c+a) = (ab + bc + ac)(abc) + (ab + bc + ca)(a+b+c) + abc \\]\n\\[\n(a+b)(b+c)(c+a) = 2 \\cdot 11 + 2 \\cdot (-3) + 11\n\\]\n\\[\n(t) = 22 - 6 + 11\n\\]\n\\[\nt = 27\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of $t$ is \\boxed{27}.",
